{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Besides the burnt-offering of the new month.</b> And if you ask: why did it not say 'and besides the sin-offering of the month'? One may answer: all the burnt-offerings have an equivalent atonement — for a positive commandment and for a negative commandment that is remittable to a positive commandment, and therefore it mentioned them one alongside the other. But the sin-offering of Rosh Chodesh and the sin-offering of Rosh HaShanah do not have equivalent atonement. How so? That of Rosh Chodesh atones for a matter where there is no awareness, neither at the beginning nor at the end, as the Sages explained, since it is written in connection with it 'לה׳' (for YHWH). But that of Rosh HaShanah atones for a matter where there is no awareness at the beginning but there is awareness at the end, and therefore it did not mention them one alongside the other." "<b>And their libations.</b> It refers to the wine libations of Rosh HaShanah, and to the wine libations and the meal-offering libations of the burnt-offering of the new month and of the daily burnt-offering."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:20:09.193576021Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}